 ],
 "text": "Uber just put 30,000 people on AI, but they didn't start with 30,000. They started with 30 engineers who sat with teams for two weeks. That's the part most companies skip. They buy the licenses and hope. Here's what works for a warehouse or an online store. Pick one team and one boring job they repeat every day. Build it with their real examples, not a demo. Give it one owner and a list of what needs a yes. Then, and only then, add the next team. At contentsystems.ai, that's how every rollout starts. Want the ownership we use? Comment Systems and we'll send it to you free."
